    "summary": "Horn‑rich Weather Report Suite, fiery Truckin' and soaring Looks Like Rain",
    "blurb": "The second set rides a horn‑driven groove highlighted by an expansive Weather Report Suite and a gripping Eyes of the World jam. Jerry’s vocals shine on Sugar Magnolia while his lead work burns through Truckin', and Keith adds a unique Theremin texture to Looks Like Rain.",
    "review": "September 17, 1973 at the Onondaga County War Memorial finds the Dead deep in their experimental stride. The first set offers solid rockers and country‑flavored numbers, but it’s the horn‑laden second half that truly stands out. A seamless Truckin' → Eyes of the World transition launches into a high‑octane jam before the band dives into the three‑part Weather Report Suite, where Jerry’s lead guitar crackles over Keith’s Theremin‑tinged intro and an expansive Let It Grow. The suite’s soaring horns lift the energy to a peak that carries through to a heartfelt Stella Blue and a jubilant Sugar Magnolia closer. Across all available soundboard sources the performance feels tight yet adventurous, with the horn section adding fresh color to classic material while the core quartet remains locked in groove.",
